#: modules/mcp/abilities/manage-revisions-ability.php:40
msgid "Undoes MCP changes to an Elementor document (page, post, template, component). Every MCP write tool returns an undo_revision_id holding the document state from before that change; action=restore with that revision_id brings back that state: the element tree, page settings and component overridable props. A restore replaces the whole document with that state, so every change made after it (including unrelated settings) is discarded; to undo several changes, restore the undo_revision_id of the earliest one. On published documents the restore is staged in a draft copy like other MCP edits: pages stay unchanged until you call elementor/publish-document, and components until you call elementor/manage-component with action=publish. The response returns a new undo_revision_id; restore it to redo the change you just undid. When the document already matches the undo point, nothing is changed (changed=false). Only undo_revision_id values returned by MCP calls can be restored, and WordPress revision limits can remove old ones (the restore then returns \"Revision not found\")."
msgstr ""

